From: mscharged-port
Subject: Competitive play: a tournament game that broke off goes on from where it was
Upstream-base: 8b9d92dd88b4c727cc6359ee4cd5ba128cced7b8

A game of a Recharged tournament set that broke off (a player closed
their game or lost the connection) is not counted: the set's next game
goes on from it, on the same sides (0079) with the same teams, from its
goals and clock. The draft takes this machine's team by itself, without
the captains' and sidekicks' screens (NetworkDraft: the captain on its
turn, the sidekicks once theirs comes). The draft host puts the goals
(home, away, once the sides are swapped) and the seconds on the clock in
the game start message (mResume, mStartScores, mStartSeconds), which every
machine takes: the match starts from them (cGame's scores, its clock and
the HUD's scores, as a Striker Challenge's start from its goals).

diff --git a/include/Game/NetworkMessages.h b/include/Game/NetworkMessages.h
index 0f8ac92..abc6b43 100644
--- a/include/Game/NetworkMessages.h
+++ b/include/Game/NetworkMessages.h
@@ -31,6 +31,11 @@ public:
     // Tweak patch 0079: the draft's two teams swap places for a set's
     // game (the draft host decides it for every machine).
     /* 0x28 */ u8 mSwapSides;
+    // Tweak patch 0080: a set's game that goes on from one that broke off
+    // starts from these goals (home, away) and seconds on its clock.
+    /* 0x29 */ u8 mResume;
+    /* 0x2A */ u8 mStartScores[2];
+    /* 0x2C */ u16 mStartSeconds;
 #endif
 };
 
